[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Sparse complex factor-correction arithmetic

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FAER-COMPLEX-CORRECTION-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Preserve the original equations across factor corrections
STATEMENT: >>>
Sparse complex iterative refinement shall submit the original residual b-A*x
to the existing factor and add the returned correction to the current values.
The candidate shall still satisfy the independent all-row acceptance bound;
the correction shall not replace or multiply the current values.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: src/backend_faer.rs refine_complex_solution, unchanged.
Verification: complex_refinement_contracts::
coupled_complex_correction_uses_original_residual_and_adds_the_delta uses
A=[[2,j],[0,3]], b=[3+7j,9-3j] and known x=[1+2j,3-j]. Independently expanded
quarter-valued residual and correction are exact in binary. The callback tests
the internal factor boundary; this is not an independent factor-library test.
Evidence: docs/faer-refinement-arithmetic-results.md and
evidence/faer-refinement-arithmetic-results.json.
<<<
